---
prompt:
  schemaStrictness: retry
output:
  schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    required: [title, branch]
    properties:
      title:
        type: string
        maxLength: 40
        description: "PR title: imperative, <=40 characters, conventional-commit style when applicable"
      body:
        type: string
        description: "Markdown body summarising what changed and why; may be empty for trivial PRs"
      branch:
        type: string
        maxLength: 40
        description: "Suggested branch name: kebab-case, <=40 chars, conventional-commit type prefix (feat/, fix/, chore/, refactor/, docs/) when the commits share a type. Use only [a-z0-9/-]"
---
You are opening a GitHub pull request for the following local commits.
Generate a concise PR title, a short markdown body, and a branch name. Return structured output matching the provided output schema.

Guidelines:
- Title: imperative mood, <= 40 characters, prefer conventional-commit style when the commits share a type and it fits naturally.
- Body: 1-4 short sections (What / Why / Notes). Bullet lists over prose. Omit sections that add no value.
- Branch: kebab-case, <= 40 characters, conventional-commit type prefix (feat/, fix/, chore/, refactor/, docs/) when the commits share a type. Use only [a-z0-9/-]. Example: "feat/user-auth-rate-limit".
- Do NOT invent context that isn't supported by the commit messages.

Commits (in order):
{{#each commits}}
--- commit {{index}} ---
{{message}}
{{#if files}}
files: {{files}}
{{/if}}

{{/each}}
